  "title": "GE Dryer",
  "revisionid": 1480044,
  "contents_raw": "== Background ==\n\nGeneral Electric (GE) is an American multinational conglomerate that was founded by Thomas Edison, Charles A. Coffin, Elihu Thomson, and Edwin J. Houston in 1892. The company began producing dryers in the 1950s.\n\nIn 2016, Haier, a Chinese multinational home appliances and consumer electronics company, acquired GE Appliances.\n\n== Identification ==\n\nGE Dryers often come equipped with SensorDry technology. The model number can be found inside the dryer, around the drum. Common models include the GTD33EASKWW, GTD72EBPNDG, and GFD55ESSNWW.\n\n== Additional Information ==\n\n* [link|https://www.geappliances.com/ge/find-model-serial-number/dryers.htm|GE Dryer Number Lookup Resource]\n* [link|https://www.geappliances.com/ge/service-and-support/literature.htm|GE Owner's Manuals]\n* ***GE Customer Support Phone Number:*** 1-800-432-2737",
